fact WorkItem(id: "WI-976", description: some(value: "SCALAND: SCOPE-HOOD IS UNTYPED, SO 'THIS TERMID IS A SCOPE' IS A CLAIM EVERY CALLER RE-MAKES AT RUNTIME. WI-962 gave 'what do we call this scope in a diagnostic' one answer (`KnowledgeBase.scopeDisplayName`, over `scopeFunctor`), but both still take a bare `TermId` and both still have a not-a-scope arm: `scopeFunctor` answers `None` and `scopeDisplayName` THROWS. That arm is unreachable in fact — `makeNameTermFromSym` is the sole producer of a scope term and builds only a nullary `Term.Fn` (WI-962 funnelled the other two producers through it) — so it is a runtime check standing in for a type. The same untyped-ness runs deeper: `SymbolTable` keys NINE methods on a raw `scopeRaw: Int` (`define`, `addExposed`, `addTypeParam`, `addImport`, `addParent`, `scope`, `scopeMut`, `resolveInScope`, `resolveRecursive`), `SymbolDef.Resolved` carries `scopeRaw: Int`, and `ScopeInclusion` carries `parentScopeRaw: Int` — so a scope, an arbitrary term, and an arbitrary integer are the same type today. WORK: an opaque `ScopeId` minted ONLY by the producer, threaded through the `SymbolTable` API; then `scopeFunctor` needs no `Option` and `scopeDisplayName` needs no throw, by construction rather than by comment. CONSIDERED AND REJECTED as the primary fix: an opaque `ScopeName = String` on `LoadError`, which would make the literal `\"requires\"` WI-962 removed a compile error — cheap (~10 lines) but it types the SYMPTOM: it equally accepts the right type of name computed from the wrong scope, which is the likelier next drift. Do it only as a rider if `ScopeId` proves too big. ACCEPTANCE: `scopeDisplayName` has no failure arm, and the deleted `IllegalStateException` has no replacement; say at the site which test fails when the change is backed out. Related: WI-962, WI-957."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "scaland-sbt-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "user", at: "2026-08-04T08:28:28Z"))

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-976", name: "scaland")
